.TH APRSLIST 1 "23 September 2011" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME 
aprslist \- Lists APRS stations heard and sends APRS beacons.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aprslist [-d] [-l] [-s] [-v]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B aprslist
Sends APRS beacons and collects information from APRS beacons. 
.P
Aprslist sends it's coordinates and Port specific information on each 
configured port.
.P
The collected information may be displayed on the local console.
.P
Received APRS info may also written to /var/ax25/aprs.dat in an ASCII 
readable form.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 20
.BI \-l
Write "starting" and the errors to the system log
.TP 20
.BI \-s
Display the stations recorded in aprs.dat and exit; nothing is sent
.TP 20
.BI \-d
Run in foreground
.TP 20
.BI \-v  
print version and exit
.TP 20
.BI \-?  
Display usage: aprslist [-l] [-s] [-d] [-v]
.P
Only one
.B aprslist
may run on a node. A second one refuses to start while the first holds the lock file
.IR /var/ax25/fpac/aprslist.lock .
The
.B \-s
mode takes no lock.
.SH FILES
.IP  "/etc/ax25/aprslist.conf  /var/ax25/aprs.dat"
(under the prefix FPAC was built with, /usr/local by default)
.SH AUTHOR
Bernard Pidoux F6BVP <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
aprslist.conf(5), /usr/local/share/doc/fpac/aprslist.txt
